red restart-protocol mutations were followed by complete recovery checks. Final lifecycle observations show no failed services, new listening ports, or unexplained temporary residue.","evidence_ids":["cmd-4492ce7c76ec4199","cmd-7be748a1827f450f","cmd-8a0522f5ca4f4127","cmd-dfd2d08bcab04898","cmd-d4a2560760354f2f","cmd-f8925cf97c3741c1","cmd-33f1d6479db046d8","cmd-6ca399f57907423c","cmd-4a7b27ff5110437e","cmd-e406f563814a4e59","cmd-838af61f737c4992","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node2:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node2:listening-sockets"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied. The evidence demonstrates scheduled nightly execution, a successful cross-node content transfer into dated archives at the required destination, and working seven-day retention. The provider-wide restart protocol is complete for both nodes: each has a healthy pre-restart state, restart acknowledgement, changed boot identity, recovered services and persistent configuration, and a successful post-restart backup. Fixed lifecycle boot identities independently corroborate both restarts.","limitations":["No naturally triggered 02:00 cron execution was captured; scheduling is supported by the installed cron entry, active/enabled crond, and repeated successful manual invocation of the exact scheduled command.","The source directory was absent initially and contained no real workload data after the transient probe was removed, so transfer fidelity was demonstrated with one test file rather than a representative production dataset.","Package-health observations timed out both before and after execution on both nodes, so package consistency could not be independently compared."]}
